# 3. Platform Operating Modes

Create a global setting called **Platform Operating Mode**.

Available options:

- eCommerce Mode.
- Product Catalogue / Inquiry Mode.

The administrator can switch modes at any time.

Both modes must use the same products, categories, variations, attributes, customers, and media library.

## 3.1 eCommerce Mode

Enable:

- Product browsing.
- Product variation selection.
- Product pricing.
- Shopping cart.
- Coupon application.
- Shipping method selection.
- Checkout.
- Guest checkout.
- Customer information.
- Cash on Delivery.
- Order confirmation.
- Order management.
- Customer order history.

## 3.2 Product Catalogue / Inquiry Mode

Enable:

- Product browsing.
- Product variation selection.
- Inquiry cart.
- Quantity selection.
- Customer inquiry form.
- Inquiry submission.
- Inquiry management.
- Quotation creation.
- Quotation communication.

Disable standard checkout and payment functionality.

The cart must become an inquiry cart.

Customers should be able to add multiple products and different product variations to the same inquiry.

The inquiry should contain:

- Product name.
- Product image.
- Product SKU.
- Selected variation.
- Quantity.
- Customer information.
- Customer message.

Allow customers to submit inquiries without creating an account.

## 3.3 Independent Feature Settings

In addition to the global operating mode, create individual settings for:

- Show or hide product prices.
- Show or hide sale prices.
- Show or hide stock availability.
- Show or hide SKUs.
- Enable or disable product inquiries.
- Enable or disable quantity selection.
- Enable or disable quotation requests.

These settings should be configurable globally, by category, and by individual product where applicable.

The global operating mode must determine the primary workflow, while individual settings control optional functionality.

