# 26. Critical Business Logic

The following requirements are mandatory:

1. Both modes must share one product database.
2. Switching modes must not delete historical data.
3. Variations must work in both modes.
4. Every variation must support independent SKU and stock.
5. Each variation can have its own price and image.
6. Prices can be hidden globally, by category, or by product.
7. The eCommerce checkout must initially support Cash on Delivery only.
8. Catalogue Mode must use an inquiry cart instead of checkout.
9. Administrators must be able to create quotations from inquiries.
10. Quotations must be convertible into orders.
11. Products must support bulk import and export.
12. All important settings must be manageable through the admin dashboard.
13. The frontend must be fully responsive.
14. SEO must be implemented throughout the application.
15. All features must be functional and connected to the database.
16. Customer and administrator workflows must be tested.
17. Product, variation, order, inquiry, and quotation history must be preserved.

